    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31271" root="عيل" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعِيلٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَائِلٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also A man <i>having a
family,</i> or <i>household;</i> and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَيَّلٌ</span></b> : (TA:) or
<i>having a numerous family</i> or <i>household;</i> and in
like manner, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, applied to a woman. (S, O,
TA.) [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عول</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, applied to a
wolf, a lion, and a leopard, <i>Seeking,</i> or <i>seeking
after,</i> prey; (K, TA;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيِّلٌ</span></b> . (TA.)

